---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="Why the Galamsey Tracker exists and where to report illegal mining in Ghana.">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Galamsey is gold mining without a licence. It strips forest, digs pits that fill with water and turns rivers brown with mud. In August 2026 the mud in the River Pra at the Daboase water treatment plant, which supplies Sekondi-Takoradi, reached more than 20 times the permitted level, and drone footage showed mining right opposite its intake (<Src id="citi-daboase-2026">Citi Newsroom</Src>).</p>
    <p>The Galamsey Tracker shows where land is being cleared, week by week, using free satellite data from NASA and the European Union's <Src id="copernicus">Copernicus programme</Src>. Nobody has to visit a site or file a report for it to appear here. The aim is that anyone, from a reporter to a district officer to someone who lives nearby, can see the same evidence and check it.</p>
    <p>It is an independent project by an ordinary citizen who cares about the problem, not a scientist or a mining expert. It relies on data and methods published by NASA and the European Space Agency, and <a href="/method">explains how it works</a> so anyone can check it. It is not connected to the government or any company.</p>
    <h2>Report illegal mining</h2>
    <p>This site cannot take reports or act on them. The government's taskforce against illegal mining is NAIMOS, under the <Src id="mlnr">Ministry of Lands and Natural Resources</Src>, and it has asked the public for information. We have not found an official reporting line we can confirm, so check any phone number with the Ministry before you rely on it.</p>
    <h2>Counting visits</h2>
    <p>We count visits with <Src id="cloudflare-web-analytics">Cloudflare Web Analytics</Src>, so we know how many people read the site and which pages they open. It uses no cookies and does not collect personal data about you.</p>
    {CONTACT_EMAIL && (
      <>
        <h2 id="help">Help improve it</h2>
        <p>The tracker misses some kinds of galamsey, such as dredging on rivers, because they do not clear land. We are looking for ways to spot them. If you have an idea, data that could help, or want to work together, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>For questions about the data, corrections or press enquiries, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. A person reads every message.</p>
      </>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: calc(68ch + 2 * var(--gutter)); padding-bottom: 24px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 32px 0 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; margin: 36px 0 10px; }
  p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
</style>
